      {
        "id": "note_format",
        "type": "flograph.util.note",
        "pos": [
          0,
          -300
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "## 1 · Table formatting  (T2, T3, V2, W1)\n\n**T3** — `20* = 1 => icon ✓ green` puts a tick in *every* 20xx column where the cell is 1. This is the line you reported as \"20* doesn't work\": the glob was always fine, but a `=>` rule could not place an icon at all.\n\n**T2** — `status colormap: fail=red, watch=amber, ok=green` replaces one condition line per value.\n\n**V2** — the card opens sorted by **revenue, descending** without anyone clicking a header. See **Sort by** in the Properties panel.\n\n**W1** — this card is **1800 × 760**. The old ceiling was 1600 × 2000; drag its corner or type into Width to go up to 4000.",
          "width": 520,
          "height": 260
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null
      },
      {
        "id": "src",
        "type": "flograph.io.table",
        "pos": [
          0,
          0
        ],
        "params": {
          "data": "{\"version\": 2, \"columns\": [{\"name\": \"region\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"name\": \"month\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"name\": \"status\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"name\": \"2023\", \"type\": \"integer\"}, {\"name\": \"2024\", \"type\": \"integer\"}, {\"name\": \"revenue\", \"type\": \"number\"}], \"rows\": [[\"South\", \"Mar\", \"ok\", 1, 0, 30.0], [\"North\", \"Mar\", \"fail\", 0, 1, 10.0], [\"South\", \"Jan\", \"watch\", 1, 1, 55.0], [\"North\", \"Jan\", \"ok\", 0, 0, 22.0], [\"East\", \"Feb\", \"fail\", 1, 1, 41.0], [\"East\", \"Jan\", \"ok\", 0, 1, 17.0], [\"West\", \"Feb\", \"watch\", 1, 0, 63.0], [\"West\", \"Mar\", \"ok\", 1, 1, 28.0]]}",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 300
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": "Source data"
      },
      {
        "id": "publish",
        "type": "flograph.util.goto",
        "pos": [
          700,
          120
        ],
        "params": {
          "name": "Source data"
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null
      },
      {
        "id": "formatted",
        "type": "flograph.viz.show_table",
        "pos": [
          920,
          -60
        ],
        "params": {
          "format_rules": "# T3 — an icon placed by a condition, across a column pattern.\n# This is the line that could not be written before.\n20*     = 1 => icon ✓ green\n\n# T2 — a value → colour map, instead of one condition line per value.\nstatus  colormap: fail=red, watch=amber, ok=green\n\n# and the same idea as a lookup, reading each column's own value\n# (T3's other half — no source column before the colon)\nrevenue scale green\n",
          "sort": "revenue",
          "sort_dir": "descending",
          "width": 1800,
          "height": 760
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": "Formatted"
      },
      {
        "id": "note_pivot",
        "type": "flograph.util.note",
        "pos": [
          0,
          900
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "## 2 · Pivot keeps your order  (X2)\n\nThe source months are **Mar, Jan, Feb** — neither alphabetical nor calendar order, so you can tell the two apart.\n\nThe **top** pivot uses the new default, *as they appear*: columns come out Mar, Jan, Feb.\n\nThe **bottom** one is set to *sorted*, the old behaviour: Feb, Jan, Mar — which is the alphabetical-months problem you hit.",
          "width": 520,
          "height": 240
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null
      },
      {
        "id": "from_pivot",
        "type": "flograph.util.goto_from",
        "pos": [
          620,
          1420
        ],
        "params": {
          "source": "publish"
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null
      },
      {
        "id": "pivot_kept",
        "type": "flograph.transform.pivot",
